1
00:00:12,470 --> 00:00:13,840
Hello.
哈囉

2
00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:18,240
Hello.
哈囉

3
00:00:18,710 --> 00:00:20,010
I love my new job!
我愛死我的新工作了！

4
00:00:20,420 --> 00:00:23,010
- Honey, you're screaming. - You bet your ass I am!
-親愛的，你在吼叫 -你說的沒錯，我就是！

5
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:25,150
I just had the best first day ever!
這工作是有史以來最棒的！

6
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,480
The kitchen? Twice as big as Allessandro's.
那個廚房，比之前的餐廳大兩倍…

7
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:29,480
Oh, that's great.
喔，太棒了

8
00:00:29,860 --> 00:00:33,950
And clean? Not just health department-clean, Monica-clean!
說到乾淨，不只是符合衛生局標準 是莫妮卡式的乾淨！

9
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:35,720
Awesome.
酷斃了

10
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:38,460
Oh, and the people are so nice.
喔，還有同事都很好

11
00:00:38,670 --> 00:00:40,730
There's this one guy, Jeffrey, he's the maitre d'.
有一個男的叫傑佛瑞 他是餐廳領班

12
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:43,040
Chandler, you will love him!
錢德，你會很喜歡他的！

13
00:00:43,240 --> 00:00:47,230
He is without a doubt the funniest guy I have ever met!
毫無疑問他是我遇過最風趣的男人了！

14
00:00:49,516 --> 00:00:51,575
The One With The Male Nanny

00:00:52,516 --> 00:00:53,575
rainystar壓制iPod-MP4

15
00:01:40,100 --> 00:01:42,790
- This is nice. - I know.
-這真棒 -我知道

16
00:01:51,870 --> 00:01:54,670
- You need both hands for that? - Yeah, I kind of do.
-你需要兩隻手才打得開？ -是啊，應該是要

17
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:56,870
Well, how's this?
嗯，那這樣呢？

18
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:09,850
Are you sure that's sweet enough?
你確定那樣夠甜嗎？

19
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:17,560
Look at you two holding hands.
瞧瞧你們兩個 手握著手

20
00:02:17,730 --> 00:02:19,630
Is this getting serious?
是不是開始認真了呢？

21
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:23,630
Have you not talked about it yet?
你們有沒有談過了呢？

22
00:02:25,470 --> 00:02:27,370
Am I making you uncomfortable?
我是不是讓你們很不舒服呢？

23
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:31,540
If you were bigger you'd hit me.
如果你再高壯一點你就會扁我了 對不對？

24
00:02:36,580 --> 00:02:37,680
I'm sorry.
不好意思

25
00:02:37,850 --> 00:02:41,750
It's obviously way too early for us to be having that conversation.
很明顯地現在就討論那種事 對我們而言是太早了

26
00:02:42,160 --> 00:02:44,090
- Is it? - Maybe not. Is it?
-會嗎？ -或許不會，會嗎？

27
00:02:45,330 --> 00:02:46,350
When I got divorced..
當我離婚後…

28
00:02:46,530 --> 00:02:49,660
I didn't think I'd feel this way about someone for a really long time.
有一段很長的時間 我不認為會對任何人有這種感覺

29
00:02:49,830 --> 00:02:52,660
Then again, I didn't think I'd meet someone like you. And..
而且，我也不認為會 遇到像你這樣的人…

30
00:02:52,830 --> 00:02:56,900
This may be crazy-soon, but I want you to have this.
這或許太瘋狂快速了 但我希望給你這個

31
00:02:58,470 --> 00:03:00,340
No, not.. That's gum.
不，不是…那是口香糖

32
00:03:02,710 --> 00:03:05,870
Oh, five bucks! I love it when that happens, you know?
喔，五塊錢！ 我超喜歡這種事發生的，你知道嗎？

33
00:03:06,050 --> 00:03:08,110
- You don't know it's there.. - I know. Keep digging.
-你不知道那裡有… -我知道，繼續挖

34
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,610
Sorry.
抱歉

35
00:03:14,190 --> 00:03:15,210
It's a key.
是一隻鑰匙

36
00:03:15,390 --> 00:03:18,760
To be honest, I think I'd prefer the five dollars.
老實說，我想我寧可要那五塊錢

37
00:03:19,990 --> 00:03:22,360
- It's to my apartment. - Wow!
-我公寓的鑰匙 -哇！

38
00:03:23,500 --> 00:03:25,020
Big step for Phoebe and Mike.
菲比跟麥克 兩人關係的一大步

39
00:03:25,200 --> 00:03:28,400
I don't want you to feel like you have to give me your key..
我不希望你覺得這樣 你也要給我你的鑰匙

40
00:03:28,770 --> 00:03:31,300
- No, I want to. - Thank God.
-不，我要 -感謝上帝

41
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:37,400
Wow. I was starting to think I'd never meet someone that..
哇，我本來還在想 我應該不會遇到一個人…

42
00:03:37,580 --> 00:03:39,380
I wanted to do this with.
讓我想要這樣做的

43
00:03:40,320 --> 00:03:41,940
Here you go.
拿去吧！

44
00:03:43,590 --> 00:03:45,820
- This is cool. - It really is.
-這太酷了 -真的是很酷

45
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:51,720
I know it. It is amazing. These little things open doors!
我知道，太驚人了 這些小東西可以把門打開！

46
00:03:55,760 --> 00:03:57,820
So I don't go back to work for another four weeks..
我四星期之後才需要回去上班…

47
00:03:58,030 --> 00:03:59,970
but we would like our nanny to start right away..
但是我們希望我們的保姆可以馬上上班

48
00:04:00,130 --> 00:04:01,900
so that Emma could get a chance to know her.
那艾□才有時間熟悉她

49
00:04:02,270 --> 00:04:04,240
I think that's really smart.
我想這樣做是很聰明的

50
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:06,770
The easier we can make the transition for her the better.
我們換手過程越流暢對她越好

51
00:04:06,940 --> 00:04:07,970
That's great. Great.
太棒了，很好

52
00:04:08,140 --> 00:04:10,510
- So do you have any questions for us? - Not really.
-那你有沒有其他的問題想問我們呢？ -沒有

53
00:04:10,680 --> 00:04:13,010
All right. Well, thank you so much for coming.
好了，那謝謝你跑這麼一趟

54
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:15,780
- Thank you. - It was really nice to meet you.
-謝謝 -很高興認識你

55
00:04:15,950 --> 00:04:18,440
- We will call you. - Oh, you know, wait.
-我們會打電話給你 -喔，等一下…

56
00:04:18,620 --> 00:04:20,320
I do have one question.
我是有一個問題

57
00:04:20,490 --> 00:04:23,460
Do you guys do random drug testing?
你們會不定期對人做毒品測試嗎？

58
00:04:25,760 --> 00:04:28,460
Boy, we hadn't really thought of that.
天啊，我們還真的沒想過這個

59
00:04:28,630 --> 00:04:32,590
That's cool. But if you do, I'm gonna need three days' notice.
沒關係，但是如果你們要求要做 我需要你們提前三天告訴我

60
00:04:32,970 --> 00:04:34,200
Okey-dokey!
好的，沒問題！

61
00:04:35,940 --> 00:04:37,460
We're never gonna find a nanny.
我們永遠都找不到保姆了

62
00:04:37,640 --> 00:04:41,170
Come on, Rach. We will. I promise. We have more interviews.
別這樣，瑞秋，我保證我們會找到的 我們還有其他的面試

63
00:04:41,340 --> 00:04:45,470
Worse comes to worst, we can always reconsider the first one we met with.
情況不可能再更糟 我們總是可以重新考慮第一個人選

64
00:04:45,850 --> 00:04:49,440
- What, the blond with no bra? - She was blond?
-什麼？那個沒穿胸罩的金髮女郎嗎？ -她的頭髮是金色的嗎？

65
00:04:52,020 --> 00:04:53,080
Just a sec.
等一下

66
00:04:53,450 --> 00:04:55,850
Okay, this one's name is Sandy.
好的，這個叫做珊帝

67
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:59,860
She's got a degree in Early Childhood Education.
她有幼兒教育學位

68
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:04,530
She worked for her last family for three years.
她在上個工作的家庭做了三年

69
00:05:06,800 --> 00:05:09,740
Hi. I'm Sandy.
嗨，我是珊帝

70
00:05:13,110 --> 00:05:15,630
And she's a little mannish.
而且她看起來有點男性化

71
00:05:23,050 --> 00:05:24,710
Oh, my God! David!
喔，我的天！大衛！

72
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:30,180
- Is this a bad time? - No, it's a great time! Come in!
-現在會打擾你嗎？ -不，現在很好！進來吧！

73
00:05:30,390 --> 00:05:32,480
Wow! Hi!
哇！嗨！

74
00:05:32,660 --> 00:05:36,220
Oh, my gosh! What are you doing here? Are you back from Minsk?
喔，天啊！你在這裡做什麼呢？ 你從明斯克回來嗎？

75
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:37,690
Just for a couple of days.
只回來幾天

76
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:40,430
I'm here to explain to the people who gave us our grant..
我是回來跟提供補助款的人解釋…

77
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:43,930
why it's a positive thing that we've spent all their money..
為什麼我們花光了所有他們給的錢…

78
00:05:44,140 --> 00:05:46,870
and accomplished nothing.
什麼都沒有做出 可以是件正面的事

79
00:05:47,540 --> 00:05:49,370
Who cares? It got you here.
誰在乎呢？反正你回來了

80
00:05:49,540 --> 00:05:52,710
It got me to New York. Then I got in a cab at the airport..
我回到紐約，然後在機場叫了部計程車

81
00:05:52,880 --> 00:05:54,540
and the guy said, "Where to?"
司機問我要去哪？

82
00:05:54,720 --> 00:05:58,520
I just gave him your address. I didn't even think about it.
我想都沒想就給了他你的地址

83
00:06:00,690 --> 00:06:02,020
Where's your luggage?
你的行李呢？

84
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,460
Damn it.
該死

85
00:06:07,060 --> 00:06:09,050
All right, I'll call the cab company.
好了，我來打電話給計程車行

86
00:06:09,330 --> 00:06:13,360
We can call them later. Can you just stand there for a moment?
我們可以等一下再打 你可以先站在那邊一下子嗎？

87
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:17,000
Boy.
天啊

88
00:06:17,170 --> 00:06:20,000
There's an old Russian expression that goes:
有一句俄羅斯老諺語是這樣的

89
00:06:24,180 --> 00:06:26,170
Roughly translated, that means:
大略的翻譯就是：

90
00:06:26,350 --> 00:06:29,610
"This thing that I'm looking at: Wow."
「我現在盯著的東西，哇！」

91
00:06:31,820 --> 00:06:33,150
Thank you.
謝謝你

92
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:36,880
You should see me when.. Actually, no, I look pretty good.
你應該看看當我… 事實上，不用，我看起來挺不錯的

93
00:06:37,960 --> 00:06:39,480
Are you kidding?
你在開玩笑嗎？

94
00:06:39,660 --> 00:06:42,320
You know, when you don't see someone for a long time..
你知道的，當很久沒有見到一個人…

95
00:06:42,500 --> 00:06:44,970
you build them up in your head, you start thinking:
你會在腦海中建立起這個人的影像 然後開始想

96
00:06:45,130 --> 00:06:47,860
"Come on, don't be crazy, nobody's that beautiful."
「少來了，別發神經了 沒有人是那樣美的」

97
00:06:48,040 --> 00:06:50,530
But, well, you are.
但是，嗯，你真的就是那樣美

98
00:06:52,470 --> 00:06:55,500
Well, so are you seeing anyone?
那麼，你現在有在跟誰交往嗎？

99
00:06:57,080 --> 00:06:58,570
No.
沒有

100
00:07:00,050 --> 00:07:02,310
I'm just the worst person ever!
我是最糟糕的人！

101
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:05,050
How can I not tell David that I'm seeing Mike?
我怎麼可以不告訴大衛 我跟麥克在一起呢？

102
00:07:05,290 --> 00:07:06,840
Maybe he didn't give you a chance.
或許他沒有給你機會說

103
00:07:07,190 --> 00:07:10,490
He said, "Are you seeing someone?" and I said, "No."
他問我有沒有跟誰交往，而我說沒有

104
00:07:11,730 --> 00:07:14,420
Well, that would've been your window.
喔，那本來是你可以澄清的機會的

105
00:07:14,930 --> 00:07:18,370
I mean, I don't know. I was looking in his eyes..
我真的不知道，我看著他的雙眼…

106
00:07:18,530 --> 00:07:22,090
and I was just thinking, "Oh, my God, it's David. David's here."
然後只能想 「我的天！是大衛，大衛在這裡」

107
00:07:22,300 --> 00:07:24,700
He's so irresistible.
他真是令人無法抗拒

108
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:28,200
- Really? The scientist guy? - Really? Chandler?
-真的嗎？那個科學家？ -真的嗎？錢德？

109
00:07:34,620 --> 00:07:36,380
Continue.
繼續說

110
00:07:37,690 --> 00:07:38,710
Then it gets worse..
然後越來越糟糕…

111
00:07:38,890 --> 00:07:40,950
because I told him I would see him tomorrow night.
因為我答應他明晚跟他見面

112
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:44,590
- Phoebe! - I know! Evil!
-菲比！ -我知道！邪惡的女人！

113
00:07:46,860 --> 00:07:52,270
I like Mike so much, you know? It's just going really well. Oh, my God!
我真的好喜歡麥克，你知道嗎？ 發展得真的很順利，我的天！

114
00:07:52,770 --> 00:07:54,790
Isn't it ironic that David would show up..
大衛出現在你跟麥克 交換鑰匙的同一天…

115
00:07:54,970 --> 00:07:57,460
on the same day that you and Mike exchange keys?
這真是很諷刺嗎？

116
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:03,370
Yeah. You know, and given my lifelong search for irony..
是啊，而且你知道我一輩子都在 找尋諷刺的事…

117
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:05,570
you can imagine how happy I am!
你可以想像的到我有多開心！

118
00:08:07,650 --> 00:08:11,140
- What are you gonna do? - I mean, I guess I just have to..
-你要怎麼辦呢？ -我想我只能…

119
00:08:11,350 --> 00:08:14,840
tell David that nothing can happen between us.
告訴大衛我們之間是不可能的

120
00:08:15,090 --> 00:08:17,280
Unless I don't.
除非我不用告訴他

121
00:08:17,460 --> 00:08:19,450
You know, complicated moral situation?
你知道的，複雜的道德情況…

122
00:08:19,630 --> 00:08:22,290
- No right, no wrong? - You have to tell David.
-是沒有錯或對 -你必須要告訴大衛

123
00:08:22,500 --> 00:08:26,260
I knew I should've had this conversation with Joey.
我就知道我應該去問喬伊才對

124
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:31,430
Funniest guy she's ever met.
她遇過最風趣的男人…

125
00:08:31,610 --> 00:08:33,670
I'm funny, right?
我很風趣，不是嗎？

126
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:36,410
What do you know? You're a door.
你知道個什麼？你只是一道門

127
00:08:36,580 --> 00:08:39,310
You just like knock-knock jokes.
你就像是「敲敲門」笑話

128
00:08:41,950 --> 00:08:44,420
Save it for inside.
等到裡面再發揮

129
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:52,190
So Oklahoma's a crazy place. You know, they call it the Sooner State.
奧克拉荷馬真是瘋狂 他們把那裡稱為早到者之州

130
00:08:52,390 --> 00:08:54,830
Frankly, I'd sooner be in any other state!
事實上，我還真希望 可以早點離開到其它的州！

131
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:59,430
And what's with Oklahoma having a panhandle?
而且奧克拉荷馬 為什麼有個平底鍋柄呢？

132
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:01,300
Can all states have stuff like that?
其它的州可以有像那樣的東西嗎？

133
00:09:01,470 --> 00:09:04,840
Hey, yeah, I'm from the waistband of Wyoming.
嘿，我是從懷俄明的中腰部來的

134
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:09,100
But when I was 7, we headed over to the crotch.
但是當我七歲的時候 我們就搬到胯下部了

135
00:09:10,650 --> 00:09:12,440
Was your cabin pressurized?
你的機艙是不是有加壓呢？

136
00:09:13,810 --> 00:09:16,840
And don't get me started on the way the people from Tulsa talk.
而且不要讓我開始告訴你們 土爾沙人說話的方式…

137
00:09:17,650 --> 00:09:18,810
Okay.
好的

138
00:09:19,950 --> 00:09:24,860
What's with the word "y'all"? You know, just two words just pushed together?
「你全」到底是個什麼字呢？ 只不過是「你們」跟「全部」加在一起

139
00:09:25,030 --> 00:09:28,720
Are we all allowed to do that? Because if so, I say why stop there?
我們可以那樣做嗎？ 因為如果可以，還有很多字可以這樣玩

140
00:09:28,930 --> 00:09:32,130
You know, your new poodle could be your noodle.
你的「新獅子狗」 可以變成你的「新獅」

141
00:09:32,370 --> 00:09:34,990
And fried chicken could be fricken.
「油炸雞塊」可以變成「炸塊」

142
00:09:35,700 --> 00:09:38,070
Waiter? Waiter, excuse me, I'll have the fricken!
服務生？服務生，不好意思 我想要點「炸塊」！

143
00:09:41,180 --> 00:09:43,540
See, that's funny with the fricken, right?
瞧，「炸塊」很好笑吧？

144
00:09:43,710 --> 00:09:47,580
No, it just reminds me of something this guy did today at work.
不，只是讓我想起今天工作時 有個人講的笑話…

145
00:09:47,750 --> 00:09:49,740
I told you about that funny guy, Jeffrey, right?
我有跟你提過一個風趣的人叫做傑佛瑞 對嗎？

146
00:09:50,220 --> 00:09:51,840
Yeah, he came up.
是啊，你提過

147
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:57,020
Well, he did this bit. You probably had to be there..
嗯，他做了一件事 你應該要在現場才感受的到…

148
00:09:57,190 --> 00:10:01,860
but it was Liza Minnelli locked in our freezer eating a raw chicken.
莉莎明妮莉被鎖在冰箱裡面吃生雞肉

149
00:10:06,770 --> 00:10:10,200
- Were you there? - No, but it sounds fricken funny.
-你在現場嗎？ -沒有，但是聽起來「炸塊」好笑

150
00:10:13,170 --> 00:10:17,170
I really understand how hard it's gotta be to leave your child with another person.
我真的可以理解要把孩子交付給 另一個人是很困難的事

151
00:10:17,350 --> 00:10:20,610
I mean, it's like leaving behind a piece of your heart.
我是說，這就像把心上的一塊肉割下

152
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:24,980
